\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Let earth and heaven combine,
\par Angels and men agree,
\par To praise in songs divine
\par The incarnate Deity,
\par Our God constracted to a span,
\par Incomprehensibly made man.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. He laid His glory by,
\par He wrapped Him in our clay;
\par Unmarked by human eye,
\par The latent Godhead lay;
\par Infant of days He here became,
\par And bore the mild Immanuel's name.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Unsearchable the love
\par That hath the Saviour brought;
\par The grace is far above
\par Or man or angel's thought;
\par Suffice for us that God we know,
\par Our God is manifest below
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Made perfect first in love,
\par And sanctified by grace,
\par We shall from earth remove,
\par And see His glorious face;
\par Then shall His love be fully showed,
\par And man shall then be lost in God.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

